 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T16:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Probably yes for a short, easy ride—if the conditions still look the same when you leave.** As of about **4:45 p.m. in Kuching on Saturday, October 17**, the latest Kuching station reading I could verify was **66 on Malaysia’s Air Pollutant Index (API), “moderate,” at noon**. That is not an evening reading, so it cannot guarantee the air will stay suitable. ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/en/stations/kuching-sarawak/))\n\nCheck the **Kuching reading on the Department of Environment’s APIMS** just before riding. If it remains **51–100**, keep the ride gentle rather than doing a long, hard workout; if it rises **above 100**, skip the outdoor ride. If you have asthma, a heart or lung condition, or the haze makes you cough or feel short of breath, choose an indoor ride instead. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Also watch the sky:** thundershowers are reported in Kuching, so don’t ride if there’s lightning or heavy rain. ",
